# Vendored upstream projects, kept locally for reading only (zengm, facesjs,
# export-faces, universal-draft-lottery-simulator). ~79MB, each with its own
# nested .git, and no runtime code depends on them — compositeRatings.js,
# draftLotteryFormats.js and faceSvgs.js only cite them in comments as the
# source of an approach. scripts/build-face-svgs.js is the one script that
# reads reference/facesjs, and its output (faceSvgs.js) is committed, so the
# game builds and runs without this directory present.
reference/

node_modules/

# The animation lab: every animation in the watched game looping side by side,
# with speed control and frame stepping. A development page, not part of the
# game — index.html never loads it and nothing at runtime references it.
#
# Kept local rather than committed, so a fresh clone gets the game and not the
# workbench. It is rebuilt by hand when needed; the animations it draws all come
# from ui/pixelSprites.js and ui/pixelMotion.js, which ARE committed, so nothing
# about it is load-bearing. See docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-15-animation-polish.md.
animation-lab.html
